.\" termux-vapt.1 — manpage
.TH TERMUX-VAPT 1 "January 2026" "termux-vapt 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termux\-vapt \- Termux Vulnerability Assessment & Penetration Testing CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termux\-vapt
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termux\-vapt
runs a 5-phase vulnerability assessment pipeline on authorized targets and produces
HTML, Markdown, and JSON reports with PoC artifacts for every confirmed finding.

Before scanning, confirm target scope, written authorization, rules of engagement,
and a stop condition. The CLI refuses to run past Phase 1 without an auth file or
interactive confirmation.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Report which tools (nmap, ffuf, sqlmap, nuclei, httpx) are installed and usable.
.TP
.BI "auth " \-f " FILE
Write or validate an authorization file for subsequent scan runs.
.TP
.BI "scan " TARGET
Run phases on TARGET. Use \-\-phase to run specific phases.
.TP
.BI "full " TARGET
Run all 5 phases end-to-end.
.TP
.BI "vuln " TARGET
Run Phase 3 (vulnerability assessment) only.
.TP
.BI "report " OUTDIR
Regenerate report.html / report.md from existing findings.jsonl files.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-phase " N
Phase number (1\-5). May be repeated.
.TP
.B "\-\-no-exploit"
Skip Phase 4 (exploitation). Read-only assessment.
.TP
.B "\-\-fast"
Skip nmap full scan. Quick phase2 with nuclei/fuzz only.
.TP
.BI "\-\-output " DIR
Output directory (default: ./output).
.TP
.BI "\-\-auth " FILE
Path to auth.json. Required before scan unless interactive confirmation is given.
.TP
.B "\-\-json"
Output findings to stdout in JSONL.

.SH OUTPUT
Output is written to the \-\-output directory:
.PP
.nf
output/
├── phase1-recon/
├── phase2-scan/
├── phase3-vuln/
├── phase4-exploit/
├── report.html
├── report.md
├── exec-summary.md
└── findings-merged.json
.fi

.SH AUTHORIZATION
Do not run against any target without written authorization from the system owner.
See docs/AUTHORIZATION.md for the full gate checklist.

.SH SAFETY
By default termux\-vapt runs read-only. Use \-\-no-exploit to skip Phase 4 entirely.
sqlmap is invoked with \-\-batch (non-interactive) and limited \-\-level/\-\-risk.
No destructive payloads, no DoS, no lateral movement.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR ffuf (1),
.BR sqlmap (1),
.BR adb (1)

